I JUST WANT TO THANK MR.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.279
ALVAREZ FOR HIS LEADERSHIP ON
THIS ISSUE

00:05:07.279 --> 00:05:10.040
AND JUST TO MOVE AND AMPLIFY
HIS COMMENT.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.230
AS HE MENTIONED IN OTAY MESA,
THERE WAS A COUPLE

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:14.210
THOUSAND CONDOMINIUMS WE'RE
TRYING TO BUILD.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.460
THIS IS THE MOST ATTAINABLE
FOR SALE

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.470
HOUSING IN THE STATE OF
CALIFORNIA.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:20.270
ABOUT HALF THE PRICE OF THE
AVERAGE

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.130
COST OF A NEW HOME IN SAN DIEGO,

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.529
AND THIS IS REPEATED THROUGHOUT
THE STATE.

00:05:24.529 --> 00:05:26.870
IT OCCURS IN THE NORTHERN PART
OF SAN DIEGO.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.180
IT OCCURS IN LA, OCCURS IN
CENTRAL VALLEY,

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.010
OCCURS IN THE EAST BAY.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.150
IT OCCURS IN SACRAMENTO.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:33.440
ALL OF OUR CONDOMINIUMS.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.350
BECAUSE OF THE NATURE OF THE
COVERAGE NEEDED,

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.610
IT'S CALLED COMMERCIAL INSURANCE

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:38.480
INSTEAD OF RESIDENTIAL

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.210
BECAUSE YOU'RE INSURING THE
ENTIRE ASSOCIATION.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.220
AND AS THE ASSEMBLY MEMBER SAID,

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.290
THE FAIR PLAN RIGHT NOW

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:48.950
DOESN'T ADDRESS MORE THAN 20
MILLION PER LOCATION.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.240
WE'RE WORKING WITH THE
DEPARTMENT TO

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.100
MOVE IT TO 20 MILLION PER
BUILDING.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.960
AND WITH THAT EXPANDED EXPOSURE,

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:54.620
WE WANT TO MAKE SURE

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.260
THE FAIR PLAN CAN HANDLE A MAJOR
LOSS,

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:58.160
THE ANALYSIS SAYS.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.480
SO ACCURATELY, THE FAIR PLAN IS

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.670
UP TO 336 BILLION IN EXPOSURE,

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:04.160
WITH 200 MILLION IN CAPACITY,

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.740
WHICH MAKES IT FISCALLY
QUESTIONABLE.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:09.950
SO GIVING THE FAIR PLAN THIS
VOLUNTARY TOOL

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.580
TO HAVE AS A BACKSTOP SHOULD A
FIRE IGNITE,

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.170
THAT BURNS DOWN A NUMBER OF
HOMES THAT

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.310
ARE INSURED BY THE FAIR PLAN.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.100
THEY HAVE THIS TOOL, TWO PIECES
OF HISTORY HERE.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.900
FOR THOSE OF US WHO'VE BEEN
AROUND A WHILE,

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.580
NOT THE FIRST TIME WE'VE DONE
THIS,

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.790
THIS COMMITTEE BACK IN 2002 WITH

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:27.500
ASSEMBLY MEMBER JUAN VARGAS,

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.540
NOW CONGRESSMAN VARGAS PASSED

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:31.190
A NEARLY IDENTICAL MEASURE

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.430
THAT ALLOWED FOR A BACKSTOP
FINANCIAL MECHANISM FOR

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:37.430
THE WORKERS COMP SYSTEM WHEN IT
RAN INTO BANKRUPTCY

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.760
AFTER THE LEGISLATURE
DEREGULATED THE COMP MARKET.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.680
SO THIS HAS BEEN TRIED AND
TESTED

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.450
VIA THE THE EYE BANK.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.460
THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THIS
IS, MR.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:49.040
ALVAREZ NOTED, IS IN THAT CASE,

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.750
THE CONSUMERS POLICYHOLDERS

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.760
PAID A $10 A YEAR SURCHARGE

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:56.510
AND THIS BILL 100% OF THE COST
OF REPAYMENT,

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:58.310
AS WELL AS DEVELOPING THE BONDS,

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.190
IS BORNE SOLELY BY THE INSURANCE
INDUSTRY.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.830
THAT'S THE ONLY DISTINCTION
BETWEEN THE TWO LAWS.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.180
UM, LAST THING I WILL SAY.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.210
THERE ARE A NUMBER OF AMENDMENTS
TAKEN ON JUNE 20TH.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.370
THEY ADDRESSED THE ISSUES THAT
WERE IN THE ASSEMBLY,

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.800
ADDRESSES THE ISSUE RAISED BY
MISS CALDERON,

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.710
AN ISSUE ALSO RAISED ON
CLARIFYING WHAT

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.810
ACTUALLY IS A FINANCIAL
INSTITUTION.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.580
WE ALSO ADDRESSED ISSUES BY THE
CALIFORNIA

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.080
DEPARTMENT OF INSURANCE,

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.150
WHO HAD QUESTIONS ABOUT USING
THE RIGHT

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.850
WORDS OF SOLVENCY VERSUS
CAPACITY.

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:28.580
WE ALSO TOOK CARE OF FAIR
PLAYING CONCERNS

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.250
ON DEFINING BOTH THE CONCEPT
OF A BOND,

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.920
BUT ALSO ADDRESSING THE ISSUE
OF A SHORT

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.410
TERM BRIDGE LOAN OR LINE OF
CREDIT.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.570
AND THE FINAL THING IS TECHNICAL
ISSUES.

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.670
WE BROUGHT IN THE LEADING BOND
COUNSEL FOR

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.860
THE TREASURER AND THE EYE BANK
WORK,

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.450
AND THEY HAVE BEEN GIVING US
TECHNICAL

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:45.950
ADVICE ON HOW TO CRAFT THIS

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:48.230
TO MAXIMIZE THE AMOUNT OF
INVESTORS

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.340
WHO WOULD CONSIDER THIS.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.950
SO THEY PROVIDE A BOND AT THE
LOWEST INTEREST RATE.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.420
THOSE ARE THE FOUR CHANGES MADE

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:55.610
SINCE THE ASSEMBLY MEMBERS.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:56.780
WE FEEL THIS IS A GOOD TOOL.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.190
IT'S NOT JUST US AT CBI.

00:07:58.190 --> 00:07:59.330
IF YOU LOOK AT THE ANALYSIS,

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.360
THERE'S CLOSE TO 30 OTHER
SUPPORTERS OF THIS.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:03.950
THIS WORKS FOR REALTORS
APARTMENT OWNERS,

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.840
BUT ALSO WORKS FOR THE FARM
BUREAU.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.520
IT WORKS FOR OTHER PARTIES THAT

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.230
ARE HAVE COMMERCIAL STRUCTURES,

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:10.010
NOT JUST US.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.410
SO WE SEE THIS AS A SOLUTION,
UH,

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.600
AVAILABLE SOLUTION TO THE FAIR
PLAN.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.100
AND WE WOULD URGE YOUR SUPPORT.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.300
THANK YOU, MADAM CHAIR.

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:19.430
YES, MA'AM.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.380
THANK YOU VERY MUCH FOR THAT
TESTIMONY.

